---
/* L45 - the same request, your machine instead of a vendor. One writer: the figures workstream F. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L45.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a boxy machine on a workbench, its power cable running to a wall socket, a round cooling fan with a turning arrow on its side, and a row of blank slips waiting in a shallow tray beside it."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L45-fig-title L45-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L45-fig-title">The same request shape, run on your own hardware</title>
      <desc id="L45-fig-desc">
        One chip at the top holds the request shape POST /v1/systemone, with two arrows dropping from it into two boxes. The left box, a hosted API, is priced per token and waits in the vendor's queue. The right box, on your own GPU, has no per-token price, runs on your own queue, and its cost is electricity. Below, a latency chart for the local run lists the requests in order: the first one is a long prussian bar labelled cold start, 40 s, and the ones after it are short bars of 236-276 ms each. A marker on the right calls the long bar the max and brackets the short ones as the p50, so the single slow outlier shows at max and not at p50.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="L45-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <rect x="40" y="28" width="560" height="28" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="320" y="47" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">one request shape: POST /v1/systemone</text>

      <path d="M 165 58 L 165 72" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L45-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 475 58 L 475 72" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L45-arrow)" />

      <rect x="40" y="76" width="250" height="100" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="56" y="102" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="12" fill="var(--color-ink)">hosted API</text>
      <text x="56" y="126" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">price per token</text>
      <text x="56" y="148" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the vendor's queue</text>
      <text x="56" y="166" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">cost = money per call</text>

      <rect x="350" y="76" width="250" height="100" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="366" y="102" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="12" fill="var(--color-prussian)">on your own GPU</text>
      <text x="366" y="126" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">no per-token price</text>
      <text x="366" y="148" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">your queue, your hardware</text>
      <text x="366" y="166" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">cost = electricity</text>

      <line x1="40" y1="192" x2="600" y2="192" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="40" y="212" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the local run, one request at a time</text>

      <text x="52" y="240" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">first</text>
      <line x1="110" y1="236" x2="560" y2="236" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <g class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 1.2s; --m-rise: 10px;">
        <rect x="110" y="228" width="300" height="16" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
        <text x="120" y="240" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-prussian)">cold start: 40 s</text>
      </g>

      <text x="52" y="272" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">second</text>
      <line x1="110" y1="268" x2="560" y2="268" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="110" y="260" width="80" height="16" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="198" y="272" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">236-276 ms</text>

      <text x="52" y="304" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">third</text>
      <line x1="110" y1="300" x2="560" y2="300" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="110" y="292" width="80" height="16" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="198" y="304" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">236-276 ms</text>

      <text x="424" y="240" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">max</text>
      <path d="M 508 258 L 508 308" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="516" y="270" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">p50</text>
      <text x="516" y="288" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the bulk</text>

      <text x="40" y="330" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one outlier: invisible at p50, obvious at max</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L45</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">The same request shape runs either in a vendor's queue for a per-token price or on your own GPU for electricity, where the first request alone pays a 40-second cold start that shows up at max and not at p50.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
